eeded to count these nouns."}}},{"id":"5b2e33f8-7bac-5d83-afec-71303930e763","topicSlug":"nouns-and-plurals","level":"A1","prompt":"Choose the verb: “These cities ____ easy to recognise.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"are"},{"id":"B","text":"is"},{"id":"C","text":"am"},{"id":"D","text":"be"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The demonstrative **these** makes the plural number explicit.","explanation":"**These cities** is plural, so use **are**.","keywords":["plural-agreement"],"skill":"plural-agreement","contextKey":"nouns-and-plurals-3","fingerprint":"659018b7cd3c0bc2013eca2610c5eab2e7b01de8fa4deb87a3c7862e097d62ea","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-nouns"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The demonstrative **these** makes the plural number explicit.","**These cities** is plural, so use **are**.","Choose **are**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**These cities** is plural, so use **are**.","B":"Is is singular and does not agree with these.","C":"Am agrees with I, not this plural noun phrase.","D":"Be is not the finite present form required here."}}},{"id":"be733720-6c1d-58fb-aed9-65d3cf868b45","topicSlug":"nouns-and-plurals","level":"A1","prompt":"Point to one item: “____ city is in the picture.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Many"},{"id":"B","text":"This"},{"id":"C","text":"These"},{"id":"D","text":"Those"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Match the demonstrative to **one** item and the singular verb is.","explanation":"The instruction specifies one city, so the singular demonstrative is **this**.","keywords":["singular-demonstrative"],"skill":"singular-demonstrative","contextKey":"nouns-and-plurals-3","fingerprint":"bf8b584e4b73ff46f1c18164da5c14814b6a4968156f7070d6b5bf9dc984d7ce","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-nouns"],"version":